WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.569 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Our next guest is
the co-founder and CMO

00:00:02.569 --> 00:00:04.304 line:92%
of the Premier Lacrosse League

00:00:04.304 --> 00:00:06.206 align:start size:94% position:6%
and current professional
lacrosse player

00:00:06.206 --> 00:00:07.574 line:92%
with the Cannons Lacrosse Club

00:00:07.574 --> 00:00:10.910 align:start size:94% position:6%
The PLL just kicked off
its third season on June 4th

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:12.545 align:start size:94% position:6%
and is available to stream
on Peacock.

00:00:12.545 --> 00:00:14.748 align:start size:94% position:6%
Please welcome to the show
Paul Rabil.

00:00:14.748 --> 00:00:17.617 align:start size:94% position:6%
♪♪♪♪
[ Applause ]

00:00:17.617 --> 00:00:19.219 align:start size:94% position:6%
Welcome, Paul.
Thank you for being here.

00:00:19.219 --> 00:00:21.021 size:81% position:41%
-Thanks for having me.
-Really appreciate it.

00:00:21.021 --> 00:00:23.289 align:start size:94% position:6%
Come on up.
-So excited to be here.

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:25.892 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is a very
big deal for us, Paul.

00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:28.161 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm just going to come
right out and let you know

00:00:28.161 --> 00:00:30.563 align:start size:94% position:6%
you are the first
professional lacrosse player

00:00:30.563 --> 00:00:31.765 line:92%
we've ever had on the show

00:00:31.765 --> 00:00:32.365 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I'm flattered.

00:00:32.365 --> 00:00:36.102
-And it's -- Now, what dre
you to playing the sport

00:00:36.102 --> 00:00:37.103 line:92%
when you were a young man?

00:00:37.103 --> 00:00:39.739
-What drew you to having a
professional lacrosse player

00:00:39.739 --> 00:00:40.273 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
on "Late Night?"

00:00:40.273 --> 00:00:42.642 size:78% position:39%
-Well, I guess that's
a bigger question.

00:00:42.642 --> 00:00:45.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I started lacrosse
when I was 12.

00:00:45.612 --> 00:00:47.213 align:start size:94% position:6%
My neighbor gave me
his backup stick.

00:00:47.213 --> 00:00:49.983 align:start size:94% position:6%
I hated it --
few people know that --

00:00:49.983 --> 00:00:51.885 line:92%
because I was pretty bad at it

00:00:51.885 --> 00:00:55.221 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then I owe my mother a
great deal of thanks,

00:00:55.221 --> 00:00:57.657 align:start size:94% position:6%
because she would
drive me to practice

00:00:57.657 --> 00:00:59.392 line:92%
for that first full year.

00:00:59.392 --> 00:01:02.162
And I was kicking and screaming.
I was crying.

00:01:02.162 --> 00:01:04.597 line:92%
I only cried, really, in sport

00:01:04.597 --> 00:01:06.132 align:start size:94% position:6%
Then I got through it,
figured it out.

00:01:06.132 --> 00:01:09.102
And I think lacrosse, whic
you'll find out in a little bit,

00:01:09.102 --> 00:01:10.303 size:84% position:42% line:92%
is like an amalgamation

00:01:10.303 --> 00:01:11.805 align:start size:94% position:6%
of all the best sports
in the world.

00:01:11.805 --> 00:01:16.376
-You -- 12 strikes me as lat
for any professional athlete

00:01:16.376 --> 00:01:17.310 line:92%
in any sport, to pick it up.

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:20.480 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is that common for people in
lacrosse or is 12 late?

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:21.014 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-12 is late.

00:01:21.014 --> 00:01:24.484
Especially nowadays, there's
a lot of sport specializatio

00:01:24.484 --> 00:01:25.085 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
in any sport.

00:01:25.085 --> 00:01:27.554 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, I grew up in Maryland,
and people consider

00:01:27.554 --> 00:01:28.555 line:92%
Maryland and New York hotbeds,

00:01:28.555 --> 00:01:31.224 align:start size:94% position:6%
but it's really
Long Island and Baltimore.

00:01:31.224 --> 00:01:31.958 size:88% position:44% line:92%
So, there wasn't much --

00:01:31.958 --> 00:01:33.460 align:start size:94% position:6%
There was no YouTube
or anything,

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:34.194 size:84% position:42% line:92%
ways to learn the game.

00:01:34.194 --> 00:01:36.429 align:start size:94% position:6%
So we all just figured it ou
with our imagination.

00:01:36.429 --> 00:01:40.533 align:start size:94% position:6%
But overall, like, getting a
opportunity to compete

00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:43.136 align:start size:94% position:6%
and have fun in a new game
and then excel.

00:01:43.136 --> 00:01:46.005 align:start size:94% position:6%
Towards the end of my career
which kind of now,

00:01:46.005 --> 00:01:49.142
as I'm 35 sitting here
like, "I'm gonna retire,"

00:01:49.142 --> 00:01:51.845 align:start size:94% position:6%
is playing the game
for a different reason.

00:01:51.845 --> 00:01:54.147 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It would be heartbreaking i
the first lacrosse player

00:01:54.147 --> 00:01:54.948 line:92%
we had on retired on our show.

00:01:54.948 --> 00:01:58.284
-Should be break this right now?
-This would be really bad.

00:01:58.284 --> 00:02:03.123
So, You -- There was an existing
lacrosse league, MLL.

00:02:03.123 --> 00:02:04.224 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-You started PLL.

00:02:04.224 --> 00:02:08.495 align:start size:94% position:6%
What inspired or what did yo
think was necessary

00:02:08.495 --> 00:02:10.563 align:start size:94% position:6%
for there to be
a new breakaway league?

00:02:10.563 --> 00:02:12.265 line:92%
-Yeah, so, again, surprise -

00:02:12.265 --> 00:02:13.967 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm the first
professional lacrosse player

00:02:13.967 --> 00:02:16.336 align:start size:94% position:6%
given that the game
had been around 20 years.

00:02:16.336 --> 00:02:18.204 align:start size:94% position:6%
But Major League Lacrosse
had existed,

00:02:18.204 --> 00:02:22.675 align:start size:94% position:6%
and our wages were, on average
$8,000 for the season.

00:02:22.675 --> 00:02:25.211 align:start size:94% position:6%
So it was a lot like
the NFL players of the '60

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:29.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
that had multiple jobs,
no healthcare, no distribution

00:02:29.182 --> 00:02:32.986 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we felt like maybe the bes
way to explain it is what

00:02:32.986 --> 00:02:35.155 line:92%
UFC did to MMA 20 years ag

00:02:35.155 --> 00:02:36.890 align:start size:94% position:6%
is what we're
hoping to do to lacrosse -

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:40.026 align:start size:94% position:6%
professionalize, commercialize
it, bring it to the masses

00:02:40.026 --> 00:02:43.663
So we did the NBC deal and w
got the games distributed.

00:02:43.663 --> 00:02:46.099 align:start size:94% position:6%
We invested in social media,
which is a big difference

00:02:46.099 --> 00:02:48.668 align:start size:94% position:6%
between starting lacrosse
in 2020

00:02:48.668 --> 00:02:50.970 align:start size:94% position:6%
versus Major League Baseball
in the 1900s,

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:54.240 align:start size:94% position:6%
where the main medium
was newspapers and radio.

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:56.276 align:start size:94% position:6%
So we have
all of these advantages

00:02:56.276 --> 00:02:58.745 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we wanted to
take advantage of those.

00:02:58.745 --> 00:02:59.679 line:92%
We increased the wage profile.

00:02:59.679 --> 00:03:01.981
We're the only team-sport
league in North America

00:03:01.981 --> 00:03:03.249 line:92%
to offer our players equity.

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:03.883 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's fantastic.

00:03:03.883 --> 00:03:06.419 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you started it
with your brother.

00:03:06.419 --> 00:03:08.788 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-How has that been?

00:03:08.788 --> 00:03:12.025
I work with my brother.
It is more upside than downside.

00:03:12.025 --> 00:03:13.393 align:start size:94% position:6%
Have you found it
to be the same?

00:03:13.393 --> 00:03:15.328 line:92%
-So, slightly more upside.

00:03:15.328 --> 00:03:17.330
The upside actually is --
so, Mike is our C.E.O.,

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:20.600
and he does a fantastic jo
running the business day-to-day.

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:24.637
But when we were building it and
we just had a five-page deck

00:03:24.637 --> 00:03:25.305 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
going to investors,

00:03:25.305 --> 00:03:28.808 align:start size:94% position:6%
trying to cobble money
together to start a league

00:03:28.808 --> 00:03:30.310 size:88% position:44% line:92%
there was so much to do.

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:32.445 line:92%
We would share hotel rooms

00:03:32.445 --> 00:03:35.281 size:84% position:42%
book them last minute
on, like, HotelTonight,

00:03:35.281 --> 00:03:36.983 line:92%
and we'd end up with a king bed.

00:03:36.983 --> 00:03:37.951 size:75% position:38% line:92%
So we'd share a bed.

00:03:37.951 --> 00:03:41.287
Can't do that with a co-founde
that you're not familiar with.

00:03:41.287 --> 00:03:41.854 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's true.

00:03:41.854 --> 00:03:44.958 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And -- But we have
a history of working together.

00:03:44.958 --> 00:03:46.292 size:78% position:39% line:92%
When we were younger,

00:03:46.292 --> 00:03:47.927 size:81% position:41% line:92%
we shoveled driveways.

00:03:47.927 --> 00:03:49.696 line:92%
We did pop-up lemonade stands.

00:03:49.696 --> 00:03:52.498 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then he uses his
hands more in manual labor

00:03:52.498 --> 00:03:55.602 align:start size:94% position:6%
He worked at a place calle
Roberts Oxygen

00:03:55.602 --> 00:03:57.237 align:start size:94% position:6%
and scooped ice cream
at Maggie Moo's.

00:03:57.237 --> 00:04:00.506 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I took my
entrepreneurial skill set

00:04:00.506 --> 00:04:01.941 line:92%
to Beanie Babies, actually

00:04:01.941 --> 00:04:03.042 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-Oh, wow! Look at that.

00:04:03.042 --> 00:04:05.345 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I was really
heavy into the trade,

00:04:05.345 --> 00:04:06.145 size:75% position:38% line:92%
had $10,000 worth of

00:04:06.145 --> 00:04:07.714 align:start size:94% position:6%
Beanie Babies
and held on to them all.

00:04:07.714 --> 00:04:09.482 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What are they worth now?
What do you think?

00:04:09.482 --> 00:04:10.316 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Zero.
-Zero dollars.

00:04:10.316 --> 00:04:11.317 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-That's good. That's good.

00:04:11.317 --> 00:04:13.720 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, that speaks well
for the future of this league.

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:14.454 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Right, right.

00:04:14.454 --> 00:04:16.055 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, so, can we
cut that segment?

00:04:16.055 --> 00:04:17.757 align:start size:94% position:6%
Our investors
are probably nervous.

00:04:17.757 --> 00:04:19.959 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The guy who was
in on Beanie Babies is now

00:04:19.959 --> 00:04:21.361 align:start size:94% position:6%
"This is the next
Beanie Babies."

00:04:21.361 --> 00:04:21.928 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Right, right.

00:04:21.928 --> 00:04:24.297 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You played in Atlanta
this week,

00:04:24.297 --> 00:04:26.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
because your league is
a touring model.

00:04:26.065 --> 00:04:26.633 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's right.

00:04:26.633 --> 00:04:29.002 size:78% position:39%
-You take eight teams
around so, you know,

00:04:29.002 --> 00:04:31.638
people in different cities
can get this experience.

00:04:31.638 --> 00:04:32.038 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Mm-hmm.

00:04:32.038 --> 00:04:34.274 size:78% position:39%
-You were in Atlanta
and on you had a clip

00:04:34.274 --> 00:04:35.475 line:92%
that made it on "SportsCenter.

00:04:35.475 --> 00:04:36.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I should note that,
in Atlanta,

00:04:36.542 --> 00:04:40.113 align:start size:94% position:6%
you guys were raising money fo
When We All Vote, is it?

00:04:40.113 --> 00:04:40.680 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's correct.

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:42.582 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And let's take a look
at this clip.

00:04:42.582 --> 00:04:43.883 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There you go.
Alright, number 9.

00:04:43.883 --> 00:04:46.653 align:start size:94% position:6%
Premier Lacrosse League --
Whipsnakes and Cannons.

00:04:46.653 --> 00:04:49.555 align:start size:94% position:6%
Paul Rabil finding
Curtis Corley.

00:04:49.555 --> 00:04:50.423 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Look at Curtis.

00:04:50.423 --> 00:04:52.358 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, the save is deflected
up in the air.

00:04:52.358 --> 00:04:54.961 line:92%
Rabil is the one who snags it.

00:04:54.961 --> 00:04:55.995 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Now, first of all,

00:04:55.995 --> 00:04:57.030 align:start size:94% position:6%
congratulations
on "SportsCenter."

00:04:57.030 --> 00:05:00.300
Second of all, why the
touring model instead of having,

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:02.635 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, eight different team
in eight different cities?

00:05:02.635 --> 00:05:05.338
-Well, what we felt like,
you know, as entrepreneurs

00:05:05.338 --> 00:05:08.174 size:81% position:41%
we needed to look at
the sport objectively.

00:05:08.174 --> 00:05:11.844
And there's 2 1/2 million
players, 10 million fans,

00:05:11.844 --> 00:05:14.681 align:start size:94% position:6%
and so to launch
this bottom-up business

00:05:14.681 --> 00:05:16.949 line:92%
in markets all over the country,

00:05:16.949 --> 00:05:18.818 align:start size:94% position:6%
we didn't think the sport
was quite there yet.

00:05:18.818 --> 00:05:20.987 align:start size:94% position:6%
But we knew with
that density of fans,

00:05:20.987 --> 00:05:23.389 align:start size:94% position:6%
that if we took the game
around the country

00:05:23.389 --> 00:05:26.392
and grew it that way, that w
would have a better chance

00:05:26.392 --> 00:05:28.661 align:start size:94% position:6%
The other thing is,
with NBC and other network

00:05:28.661 --> 00:05:30.763 line:92%
we were pitching at the time

00:05:30.763 --> 00:05:32.598 align:start size:94% position:6%
distribution
and programming windows

00:05:32.598 --> 00:05:34.500 line:92%
are really difficult to secure

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:36.536 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, in team sports,
you have this

00:05:36.536 --> 00:05:37.804 line:92%
home-and-away schedule model

00:05:37.804 --> 00:05:39.939
And we didn't want to deal
with the nuance of that.

00:05:39.939 --> 00:05:41.007 align:start size:94% position:6%
So we went to
the network and said,

00:05:41.007 --> 00:05:44.977
"What are your free window
on NBC and NBC Sports?" --

00:05:44.977 --> 00:05:46.145 align:start size:94% position:6%
that are available,
I should say.

00:05:46.145 --> 00:05:48.147
And they said, "This time on
Saturday, this time on Sunday.

00:05:48.147 --> 00:05:49.082 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm like, "Great.
We'll book them."

00:05:49.082 --> 00:05:51.217 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because we take over the venue
for the whole weekend,

00:05:51.217 --> 00:05:53.386 align:start size:94% position:6%
so it's kind of
an inside-out approach.

00:05:53.386 --> 00:05:56.489 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I do think, in the future,
we will be city-based.

00:05:56.489 --> 00:05:57.056 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's exciting.

00:05:57.056 --> 00:05:59.659 align:start size:94% position:6%
I do want to take advantag
of having you here...

00:05:59.659 --> 00:06:00.093 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Okay.

00:06:00.093 --> 00:06:01.461 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...for a little bit
of a tutorial.

00:06:01.461 --> 00:06:02.862 align:start size:94% position:6%
We have a couple of
sticks behind you.

00:06:02.862 --> 00:06:04.731 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, we do.
-And here we go.

00:06:04.731 --> 00:06:08.601
Okay, so, yeah, actually,
I brought this one for you

00:06:08.601 --> 00:06:10.036 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, great.
-This is my game stick...

00:06:10.036 --> 00:06:11.938 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, great.
-...we saw that highlight on

00:06:11.938 --> 00:06:14.006 align:start size:94% position:6%
So hopefully I can
do something like that here.

00:06:14.006 --> 00:06:17.009 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I feel like my crew
has insulted me

00:06:17.009 --> 00:06:19.045 align:start size:94% position:6%
by how close they've
put this goal.

00:06:19.045 --> 00:06:21.447 size:78% position:39%
-Yeah, this is, like,
what we would call

00:06:21.447 --> 00:06:22.682 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
a crease attackman.

00:06:22.682 --> 00:06:23.116 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Okay.

00:06:23.116 --> 00:06:24.617 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So you can shoot and scor
from here.

00:06:24.617 --> 00:06:26.185 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think I was there.
-Okay.

00:06:26.185 --> 00:06:28.054 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But we talked
a little bit backstage.

00:06:28.054 --> 00:06:30.089 align:start size:94% position:6%
You grew up in New Hampshire
You went to Northwestern.

00:06:30.089 --> 00:06:32.458 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, shout-out to the
Northwestern women's team.

00:06:32.458 --> 00:06:34.527 size:78% position:39%
-Thank you very much.
-They're really good.

00:06:34.527 --> 00:06:36.028 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'll pass that on to them
-Yeah.

00:06:36.028 --> 00:06:40.099 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I should point out
that I am not a good athlete

00:06:40.099 --> 00:06:42.201 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I'm an
excellent impressionist.

00:06:42.201 --> 00:06:43.469 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I feel like I'm
just going to follow

00:06:43.469 --> 00:06:45.004 align:start size:94% position:6%
what you do,
and this should work out great

00:06:45.004 --> 00:06:45.671 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-Well, it's obvious.

00:06:45.671 --> 00:06:47.440 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, your hand position
was already right.

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:48.474 line:92%
So that's, like, the first step.

00:06:48.474 --> 00:06:49.475 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we do
what's called cradling.

00:06:49.475 --> 00:06:52.478 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, basically,
to keep the ball in the net,

00:06:52.478 --> 00:06:54.447 align:start size:94% position:6%
you have to cradle
in this motion.

00:06:54.447 --> 00:06:55.348 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-So, you got it there.

00:06:55.348 --> 00:06:57.650 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, as you get
a little bit more talented

00:06:57.650 --> 00:06:58.618 size:88% position:44% line:92%
you can one-hand cradle.

00:06:58.618 --> 00:06:59.852 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh-huh.
-You can spin the stick.

00:06:59.852 --> 00:07:01.721 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay.
-You can drop it in one hand

00:07:01.721 --> 00:07:04.190 align:start size:94% position:6%
You can try the stick trick,
like that.

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:06.192 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sure, sure, sure, sure.
-Almost.

